Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work, free of
                      charge, if Your use is Individual Use, Educational and
                      Research Use, Non-Profit Use, Public-Sector Use or Small
                      Business Use, each as defined below. Any other production
                      use requires a commercial license from the Licensor.

                      "Individual Use" means use by a natural person on his or
                      her own account, including as a freelancer or consultant.
                      It includes use through a business entity only if the
                      entity has no employees and, together with its affiliates,
                      is within both limits of Small Business Use, tested in the
                      same way. Contractors engaged for a specific project are
                      not employees. Individual Use does not include use for the
                      internal operations of an employer or of a client. Running
                      the Licensed Work as a continuing service or pipeline for
                      the internal operations of another organization is that
                      organization's use, on whatever systems it runs, unless it
                      is part of a product or service of Your own described in
                      the paragraph on products below. Using the Licensed Work
                      to prepare documents or other deliverables for clients,
                      one job at a time, is Individual Use. A sole
                      proprietorship with no employees is the natural person
                      who owns it, and its use is Individual Use. Individual
                      Use never includes a Competing Offering.

                      "Educational and Research Use" means use by an accredited
                      school, college or university, or by its students and
                      staff, for teaching, learning or non-commercial academic
                      research.

                      "Non-Profit Use" means use by a Qualifying Non-Profit in
                      furtherance of its exempt purposes, and not in connection
                      with the sale of products or services (other than fees
                      that only recover the cost of its charitable activities).
                      A "Qualifying Non-Profit" is an organization that is
                      organized and operated exclusively for charitable,
                      educational, religious, scientific or similar
                      public-benefit purposes, whose net earnings do not
                      benefit any private person, and that is recognized as a
                      charity or as exempt from income tax on that basis under
                      the law of its jurisdiction (for example, under Section
                      501(c)(3) of the U.S. Internal Revenue Code, or as a
                      charity registered in the United Kingdom).

                      "Public-Sector Use" means use by a government department,
                      agency, municipality or other public authority for its
                      governmental functions. It does not include use by a
                      state-owned or government-controlled enterprise, or by
                      any body that sells products or services on a commercial
                      basis. Fees charged only to recover the cost of statutory
                      services are not a commercial basis.

                      Any organization that is not described in Individual Use,
                      Educational and Research Use, Non-Profit Use or
                      Public-Sector Use, including a company, partnership or
                      other business (with or without employees) and any
                      state-owned or government-controlled enterprise, is a
                      "For-Profit Organization". Production use by or for a
                      For-Profit Organization requires a commercial license
                      unless it is Small Business Use.

                      "Small Business Use" means use by a For-Profit
                      Organization that, counting its affiliates together with
                      it, had in its last completed fiscal year both (a) total
                      gross revenue below USD 1,000,000 and (b) fewer than 10
                      people working for it, or that has not yet completed a
                      fiscal year and reasonably expects to meet both limits in
                      its first one. The people working
                      for it are its employees, its owners and partners who work
                      in it, and the individuals who work for it on a regular
                      basis as contractors, counted as individuals and not as
                      companies. Revenue in another currency is converted into
                      US dollars at the exchange rate on the last day of the
                      fiscal year. An "affiliate" is any entity that controls,
                      is controlled by, or is under common control with another
                      entity. "Control" means owning more than 50% of the voting
                      interests of an entity, or having the power, by contract
                      or otherwise, to direct its management or policies.
                      Customary minority-investor rights, such as a board seat
                      or consent rights over a financing or a sale of the
                      company, held with 50% or less of the voting interests,
                      are not control, and companies that share only such an
                      investor are not under common control.
                      Entities that are controlled by the same person, or by
                      persons acting together, are under common control. An
                      arrangement whose main purpose is to bring an organization
                      within a category above, or to keep it under the limits of
                      Small Business Use, is disregarded.

                      Small Business Use includes using the Licensed Work as a
                      component of a product or service of Your own that has
                      substantial functionality beyond that of the Licensed
                      Work. Individual Use includes this only if Your business,
                      together with its affiliates, is within both limits of
                      Small Business Use, tested in the same way. A business
                      includes a sole proprietorship. A natural person's own
                      work, such as preparing reports or documents for
                      themselves or for clients, is not offering a product or
                      service to others, and these limits do not apply to it.
                      Your customers and users may use the Licensed Work only
                      as part of that product or service. If the Licensed Work
                      is not delivered as part of Your product, for example
                      because users install it themselves, each user's use of
                      it is governed by that user's own category. A product or
                      service includes software that You make available free
                      of charge.

                      No category above includes a Competing Offering, which
                      always requires a commercial license. A "Competing
                      Offering" is a product or service offered to third parties
                      whose value consists mainly of the functionality of the
                      Licensed Work. It includes hosting the Licensed Work as a
                      service for others; making the operations, commands, API
                      or tools of the Licensed Work available to third parties
                      as a service in itself, directly or through a thin
                      interface, for example through a public API or MCP
                      endpoint whose main purpose is access to the Licensed
                      Work; a desktop, web or other editor or application whose
                      value is mainly the document functionality of the
                      Licensed Work; and selling the Licensed Work, or a
                      product or service whose value is mainly the Licensed
                      Work, whether or not under another name. A product or
                      service is a Competing Offering if (a) most of what its
                      customers pay for, or use it for, is the document
                      functionality of the Licensed Work; (b) little of it
                      would remain without the Licensed Work, where an
                      interface, login, billing, prompts or similar layers
                      around the operations of the Licensed Work are not
                      features of its own; or (c) its main purpose is to let
                      third parties reach the operations, commands, API or
                      tools of the Licensed Work. A product or service that
                      uses the Licensed Work to implement substantial features
                      of its own is not a Competing Offering. This includes an
                      AI agent or an agent platform that uses the Licensed Work
                      as one of its tools: it is a product of Your own under
                      the paragraph above, and it needs a commercial license
                      once the limits of Small Business Use are reached.

                      You may copy, modify and redistribute the Licensed Work
                      free of charge, modified or not, provided that every copy
                      keeps this License and the copyright and license notices.

                      If You stop qualifying for a category above, You may
                      continue Your existing use for 90 days, and must then
                      obtain a commercial license or stop. For Small Business
                      Use, You stop qualifying on the first day after the
                      fiscal year in which You passed a limit. This does not
                      apply to an organization that stopped qualifying because
                      of an arrangement that is disregarded above.

                      "Production use" means any use of the Licensed Work other
                      than non-production use, including making it part of a
                      product or service that You provide to others.
                      Non-production use (including evaluation, development,
                      testing and demonstration) is permitted by this License
                      without any category. Use is not non-production use merely
                      because it is called a pilot, test or staging use:
                      processing an organization's real documents as part of its
                      regular operations is production use, however the
                      environment is named. Documents and other output that You
                      create with the Licensed Work belong to You, and this
                      License places no restriction on them.

